<title>JAPAN: Japan firms to revamp Ukraine oil refinery.</title>
<headline>Japan firms to revamp Ukraine oil refinery.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mitsui &amp; Co Ltd, a leading Japanese trading house, said on Wednesday that it and engineering firm Ukraine.</p>
<p>The work by the companies on the refinery owned by Ukrtatnafta in Kremenchug, central Ukraine, would include revamping a fluid catalytic cracker to enhance the gasoline yield to an annual 1.3 million tonnes from the current 800,000 tonnes, Mitsui said in a statement.</p>
<p>Trade insurance would be supplied by Japan's Trade Ministry's and the project financed through loans by the Export-Import Bank of Japan, the statement said.</p>
</text>
